  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_2bb63455e4bc43e499c3dbb9d5d98f0a",
      "statement": "The Runnable interface is the foundational execution abstraction in LangChain that defines a unified, composable protocol for synchronous invoke, asynchronous invoke, batch processing, streaming, and schema introspection across all LangChain components. The LangChain Expression Language (LCEL) leverages Runnables to enable declarative composition with operators and methods for sequential piping, parallel forking, branching, fallback, and retry logic.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L134-L350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c726e66dec3c2d0789041d63f17d399bc3d85356101fb5337df60327e64009e0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c40f00a113b34d2f9a4978eba971a71e",
      "statement": "The Runnable.invoke(input, config=None) method is the abstract core method that all Runnable subclasses must implement, transforming a single input synchronously and accepting optional RunnableConfig for execution control. All other execution methods (batch, stream, async variants) have default implementations that subclasses can override for optimization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L949-L971",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8a498a830f1cfc3b39755c123255b0f120de81bebd403f4703be0e7850bf24a9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0afd1fb343f04dbaa7abaf0bd55b0818",
      "statement": "The Runnable.batch(inputs, config=None, return_exceptions=False) method processes multiple inputs in parallel, with default implementation calling invoke for each input via ThreadPoolExecutor. Subclasses override for batching-aware backends. Batch respects per-input or single config application and optionally returns exceptions instead of raising.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L995-L1044",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b05328e8f48f44f2e15130e4d359fead12e704b1d288e8a7d108ed37db2a1bd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_018463728c0d4628b34a2f997ffc2b43",
      "statement": "The Runnable.stream(input, config=None) method yields partial outputs as they are produced, with default implementation yielding a single complete output from invoke(). Streaming components override to yield incremental outputs (tokens, chunks). The transform(input_iterator) method enables progressive end-to-end streaming through chains by mapping input iterators to output iterators without blocking on full input.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L1258-L1278",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7c6f4a12e673ac8dc3db5eaef8932f30f652751b8bfd85dc1e02ef2d7b1324f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L1824-L1862",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d0bd19ce086f6fbd1e704e70e74cb6fb78e5c48f984c1f18810f021b0824e71:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3e59655e692a4e84aad6c37f62bfa695",
      "statement": "Async execution methods ainvoke, abatch, astream, and atransform provide native async support with default implementations delegating to sync via run_in_executor or asyncio.gather. Subclasses override for native async (API calls, async database queries). All async batch methods respect max_concurrency config for controlling parallelism.",
      "evidence": [
