    },
    {
      "id": "claim_80e922ff2f2648c7b57a85ffabac75bc",
      "statement": "RunnableBranch selects and executes one of several branches based on condition evaluation. Constructor accepts variable tuples of (condition, runnable) plus optional default runnable. Conditions evaluated sequentially as Runnables returning bool; first matching condition's runnable executes. Supports both sync and async conditions/runnables natively.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/branch.py#L43-L290",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77b53fbabf2bdae2e052b15b90650cf13e0e2d73221231eb5f782f4a5b5445ed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ee808bf3084c433d809abbcca4e21933",
      "statement": "RunnableWithFallbacks executes primary runnable, then fallbacks in sequence until one succeeds. Catches exceptions matching exceptions_to_handle (default Exception); other exceptions raise immediately. Optionally injects caught exceptions into input dict before next fallback. Batch handling tracks per-input success and retries only failed inputs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/fallbacks.py#L37-L590",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a9f0c0e55d40ef5e37229535b9d3b42ed1860dee6a6511d13934e69d3f272c2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8180c955740f45cd83e610e59a776bad",
      "statement": "Runnable.with_retry(retry_if_exception_type, stop_after_attempt, wait_exponential_jitter, exponential_jitter_params) adds exponential backoff retry logic. Exception filtering is tuple of types or callable predicate. Batch retries only failed inputs. Stream and transform are not retried (ambiguous semantics). Best applied to individual components rather than entire chains.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/base.py#L2153-L2219",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b567916fd536ca00658da68bbe7043da4cc1a41e17193d3d9f0842c33105ae4e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f0f6ab25d12f44279c8b98858fa38121",
      "statement": "RunnableConfig is a TypedDict carrying execution context: tags (list), metadata (dict), callbacks (handlers), run_name, max_concurrency (int|None), recursion_limit (default 25), configurable (dict of parameter overrides), run_id (UUID). Config is threaded through child runnables via explicit parameters and context variables. merge_configs combines parent/child with child precedence and list concatenation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/runnables/config.py#L57-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:def5c5af24438aa68655c3dd7c5616745bc16d1e92d9f85b281622790264a60d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6e6dd7e03fd944a29eabd6a24a610b30",
      "statement": "configurable_fields(**fields) marks Runnable fields as runtime-configurable via ConfigurableField specifications. Fields appear in config_schema() and their runtime values are supplied in RunnableConfig.configurable dict. Enables dynamic behavior modification without reconstruction. configurable_alternatives() variant allows selecting implementations at runtime.",
      "evidence": [
